Backdrop blur in the scene graph, and blending as sway does.

wlr_scene_node_set_backdrop_blur marks a node, and each buffer under it is
drawn over a dual-filter blur of what is behind it (swayfx's algorithm and
finish), clipped to where the buffer is not transparent. On Vulkan each step
is one draw of a new blur shader; elsewhere it is built from texture draws.
Its state lives in addons, so the structs bindings mirror keep their layout.

The Vulkan renderer's blend image now holds sRGB-encoded values, so
translucent surfaces blend as on GLES and in sway rather than in linear
light, which lets far too much of what is behind show through dark
translucency. The output pass decodes before its colour transform.

